1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,999
[Music] My name is Princey Varghese, and this is my husband, Jince.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,999
We are from a place called Kolenchery in Ernakulam district. I am a nurse, and I was working in Israel.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,999
It has been 13 years this month since I started working there.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:41,999
When my daughter was just one year and a 3 months old, I went to Israel. My husband and daughter were at home. I was living alone there.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,999
For the past two to three years, I’ve had this thought in my heart—O Mother Mary, thank You!

6
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,999
I’m so grateful that God gave me the grace to come to this altar and give this testimony. I can’t express how much joy that brings me.

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,999
I am standing here today only because of the grace of Mother Mary and Jesus—thousands and thousands of thanks to them!

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:13,999
My second son, Jeron Jince, was born in Israel, in Tel Aviv. He is now two and a half years old.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,999
After he was born, and about three and a half months had passed, we had to bring him back to India

10
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,999
because, according to the law in Israel, we cannot keep a baby there for more than 3.5 months

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,999
It wasn’t possible—citizenship there is only given to Jewish people.

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:40,999
That made me feel very distressed in my heart. I cried out to God: “Lord, all these years I couldn’t raise my elder daughter myself…”

13
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,999
And now, when I finally have a son, I can’t even keep him with me.

14
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,999
I was upset thinking, “I have to stay away from both my children again.”

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:00,999
After that, a new desire came into my heart—that somehow, my family and I could go to another country, a better country.

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,999
That longing passed through my heart. My friend Anitha is in Australia. She told me:

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,999
“Why don’t you write the PTE exam?” But I told her, “I don’t have the confidence. I haven’t written English in so long. Even if I write it, I might not pass.

18
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,999
Why should I go through the pain of failing?” I didn’t have the courage to even try.

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,999
But she insisted a lot: “Just write it once. Maybe God will grant it to you.”

20
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:34,999
For 12 years, I had only been living a routine life—not in any deep faith. I was just working regularly.

21
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,999
I would only pray basic things: “Lord, please protect me. Keep me safe.” That was the only kind of direct conversation I had with God.

22
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:48,999
I was not someone who used to call on Mother Mary a lot. I am someone who belongs to the Jacobite Church.

23
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,999
We do believe in Mother Mary, but we weren’t used to calling on her so much.

24
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:01,999
It was during that time, when my heart was so burdened, that I wrote the PTE exam—and somehow, by God’s grace, I got a good score.

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:09,999
I received an Australian qualifying score. I was so happy—I felt like, “Yes, I do have some ability. I can manage English.”

26
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:16,999
At that point I felt, "I should’ve taken this exam a little earlier." That thought came to me.

27
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:22,999
With that thought, I decided to move forward. I started looking into Australian immigration through agencies. I was about to turn 39.

28
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:30,999
Everyone told me, “You should have started this earlier. Why are you trying at this age?”

29
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,999
“It’s going to be difficult now. At least a study visa could have been an option if you had tried before 35.”

30
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,999
That made me feel like my dream had ended.

31
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:48,999
Continuing to live alone in Israel, away from my children, wasn’t going to be easy anymore.

32
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,999
Even though I had a husband, it was really hard for him to handle the children alone.

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,999
He said, “We must try somehow. Let’s do whatever is needed.”

34
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:08,999
That’s when my good friend Shanty, who had taken a covenant here at Kreupasanam for her daughter to go to Australia—I knew about it—

35
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:17,999
She hadn’t expected to get it. But miraculously, her daughter Lismi got it.

36
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:27,999
That really impacted me. I thought, “If they received it, maybe through the intercession of this Mother, she could ask Jesus for mine too…”

37
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:33,999
“Maybe what didn’t happen before might be possible now.” So I thought, “Let me also try.”

38
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:41,999
That’s when my friend Jincy said, “Chechi, I’m coming to see you.”

39
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:49,999
She came to me one day, prayed, anointed my forehead with the Kreupasanam holy oil, and said:

40
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:56,999
“Chechi, it’s been so long, hasn’t it? You should try to live as a family now. Be with your children.”

41
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,999
“You’ve been separated from them for so long. It’s time to be united.”

42
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:08,999
I said, “I don’t know whether all this will actually work, Jincy.” But she said:

43
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:15,999
“Chechi, I’m telling you — if Kreupasanam Matha doesn’t do this for you, I’ll take responsibility for it. That will never happen.

44
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:20,999
I have so much faith. Have you seen Matha (Our Lady) yourself, Chechi?”

45
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,999
I told her, “Jincy, I’m not someone with that kind of deep faith. But okay, let’s try.”

46
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:39,999
All I had heard about Kreupasanam was some strange story—that someone’s vehicle stopped, and instead of diesel, they tore up paper and put it in… something bizarre like that.

47
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,999
That was the kind of negative comment I had heard.

48
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:49,999
I didn’t know whether this place was even a good or holy place. I hadn’t taken it seriously.

49
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:57,999
Two days later, I had a dream. A woman appeared—someone who looked like Mother Mary.

50
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,999
But I couldn’t fully believe it was Mother Mary.

51
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,999
While I was lying down asleep, she gently moved from above my head, down the side of my body, along the edge of the bed...

52
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,999
She was moving—passing by me, looked straight at me, and smiled.

53
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,999
She smiled at me like that, and then walked ahead and entered through the door of that room.

54
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,999
At that same moment, I saw my uncle—my father’s elder brother.

55
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:26,999
That is, my "appachan" who passed away many years ago. I had never seen him before in real life.

56
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,999
In the dream, he spoke to me and said, “Princey, everything will be alright.”

57
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:35,999
I thought, if my appachan came to tell me that everything will be fine, there must be something to this.

58
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:41,999
That must have been the Mother herself. But I still couldn’t believe it. I didn’t tell anyone about this for two days—

59
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,999
Not even my husband, not anyone in my family.

60
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:50,999
But after that, I couldn't hold it in anymore. I called Jincy and said, “Jincy, I saw a dream.”

61
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:57,999
“A woman who looked like Mother Mary came near me like this. I also saw my appachan in the dream.”

62
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:04,999
“He told me everything will be alright. And I know we were distant for years. I know the reason for that rift.”

63
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,999
“I’ll tell you about it,” I said.

64
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:13,999
Jincy replied, “Chechi, that is the Mother.

65
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,999
The thing you're praying for — Mother Mary will do it for you. Just try, chechi.”

66
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,999
“This year, you’ll go somewhere as a family. You’ll go together. Just watch,” she said.

67
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,999
Seeing Jincy’s faith—after hearing all that—I truly felt amazed.

68
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,999
I started to feel confident that there really was something in all this.

69
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:38,999
After that, I asked Jincy about how to make the covenant. I understood it from her.

70
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,999
Like I told you before, I also spoke to my friend Shanty and asked her about it too.

71
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,999
I came to understand what all had to be done. I then made the covenant online.

72
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,999
From then on, I started praying both in the morning and evening.

73
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,999
It had been around 12 years since I read the Bible regularly.

74
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:04,999
I used to read it only when I came home on leave. But now, I took the Bible app on my phone and started reading it every single day without fail.

75
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:12,999
Back in my Plus Two (Class 12) days, I had once won third prize in a story-writing competition.

76
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,999
That was during my school days—things I had completely forgotten.

77
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:21,999
Then I remembered what my father had always told me: “You should do something unique.”

78
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:27,999
Like Fr. Joseph always said—"Do something different if you can.” So I thought, let me try something.

79
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:34,999
I decided to write a song. I don’t know how to sing. I know my voice is not that great.

80
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:39,999
But I thought—it’s only Mother Mary and Jesus who are going to hear it. No one else.

81
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:44,999
So I wrote it like a song. I didn’t have time to sing it. So I just wrote it down—

82
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:53,999
Just a small song, maybe five or eight lines. And from that day onward, I began to say that song every single day.

83
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,999
I began singing that song as a prayer.

84
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:05,999
About a week after that, I spoke to an agency about my papers for New Zealand.

85
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:12,999
I prepared everything needed to submit. That’s when I realized—

86
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:19,999
Back in 2008, I had one year of nursing experience in Mumbai. To prove that experience strongly,

87
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:25,999
I needed to show salary transaction papers from that time.

88
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:34,999
So I contacted the bank in Mumbai. I called the manager and explained everything.

89
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,999
But he didn’t seem to care much—just said, “Okay, we’ll see.”

90
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:44,999
I tried everything—emails, follow-ups—but so much time passed.

91
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,999
I almost decided to drop the idea, but after taking the Kreupasanam covenant, I had gained courage.

92
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,999
I told my husband, “Can you check with the local bank once? Maybe they can do something.

93
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,999
If Mother Mary helps us, maybe it will happen.”

94
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:03,999
My husband went to the bank and spoke with them—and by God’s grace, through the power of the covenant,

95
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:11,999
the same manager who once said it wouldn’t be possible gave me the 2008 salary transaction papers within 24 hours.

96
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:19,999
When I received that paper, I was convinced—God will do this for me.

97
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:25,999
I kept praying without giving up. I told my husband, “You also pray.” I told my kids, “Pray together with us.”

98
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,999
“Let’s move forward in this covenant. Mother Mary is working wonders—

99
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,999
and I believe God will surely do this for us.”

100
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,999
All the agencies had said it wouldn’t work. But I believed—it will.

101
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:42,999
So I continued faithfully in prayer with the covenant. My husband and kids prayed from home.

102
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:49,999
After about two to three weeks, an agency named Jubilich said, “Okay, we’ll try.”

103
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:55,999
They tried with all my documents. After submitting everything, they filed for the visa.

104
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:01,999
All the financial papers were submitted. Then the agency person said,

105
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,999
“Sorry, madam, this is difficult. Even with all this financial proof, it’s not enough.”

106
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:11,999
“New Zealand and Australia have a lot of challenges.

107
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,999
It’s not like what you think. Try the UK, Malta, or maybe even Georgia—just change your plan.”

108
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:25,999
But I said, “No, I want to go to New Zealand. That’s my desire.

109
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:30,999
I feel like that’s a place where I can live happily with my family in a good way.

110
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,999
I truly feel that’s where I should go.”

111
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,999
My friend also told me, “New Zealand is a good place.”

112
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:43,999
I did some research and realized it’s actually a good place. Even in the future, it’s a country from where you can go to Australia if needed. So I said, “That’s enough for me.”

113
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,999
But they told me, “Madam, sorry, it’s hard for us to even say this…

114
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:53,999
If we submit your file, our visa success rate will drop.”

115
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,999
“First of all, you are already 39, soon turning 40.

116
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,999
At this age, once we submit the visa, there is a 99.9% chance it will be rejected.”

117
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:10,999
I told them, “I’ve made a covenant. Even if you don’t believe there’s even a 0.1% chance,

118
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:19,999
I believe that through Kreupasanam Mother Mary, this will happen. Please just try submitting it.

119
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,999
If it doesn’t get approved, then I will accept that it wasn’t God’s will for me.

120
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:29,999
Maybe it’s my fate to live here alone. Or else, I will go back to India, and live peacefully in a small way with my family.”

121
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,999
That’s what I told them after thinking it through.

122
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,999
Then the agency people said, “Madam, it’s very difficult. Why are you taking this risk when the visa success rate is practically zero?

123
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,999
It’s hard for us too.”

124
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,999
I said, “No, I won’t back down. If you stop me here, it will feel like you’re stabbing me in the heart.

125
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,999
This must go forward. Mother Mary will make this happen for me. Kreupasanam Mother never fails.

126
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,999
Jesus will do this for me through her intercession.”

127
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,999
Hearing that, and having no way to convince me otherwise,

128
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:02,999
they submitted the visa papers—despite telling me there was absolutely no chance.

129
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:07,999
But due to all these conversations and back-and-forth, there was a delay in submission.

130
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,999
My medical check-up deadline had already passed. I ended up submitting two days late.

131
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:16,999
Normally, if you submit after the medical deadline:

132
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:21,999
First, there’s a high chance of immediate rejection.

133
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,999
Second, even if they mistakenly accept the application, they will ask you to redo the medical.

134
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:31,999
But I had already spent nearly 50000 rupees in Israel on that medical check-up.

135
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,999
That money would go to waste if I had to do it again.

136
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:41,999
For a visa that may not even be approved, I would again have to submit a hefty immigration fee.

137
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,999
Plus, I had to show a large fund balance in my bank account.

138
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,999
It was a huge financial and emotional struggle.

139
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,999
The bank manager also helped me a lot—

140
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,999
all of this was truly a miracle from Kreupasanam Mother.

141
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,999
I don’t have time to explain everything here.

142
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,999
So I’ll just say this briefly—I forced them to submit it.

143
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,999
It was truly a miracle of God.

144
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,999
There is nothing that Mother Mary cannot do. Praise be to Jesus!

145
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,999
I got the visa.

146
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,999
I received the visa first—before so many younger, more qualified,

147
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:23,999
and more talented people than me, who had applied.

148
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:35,999
The name of that girl (from the agency) was Sindhu. She had been deeply upset, saying it wasn’t even possible to submit my visa file.

149
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:40,999
She had worked so many days on my file and still couldn’t submit it. But when they came to know that I got the visa —

150
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:49,999
— all of them cried. Everyone in that agency realized what the power of Kreupasanam Mother really is. They understood the power of Jesus.

151
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:57,999
They said to me: “Princey, this is something that never happens. What has happened for you is beyond explanation.

152
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:06,999
A student visa at age 39 — after doing GNM (General Nursing and Midwifery), with credit issues, and your health check-up dates already expired —

153
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:15,999
for someone in that situation to get a visa... this is nothing short of a miracle. This happened only by the miraculous grace of God.”

154
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,999
They acknowledged it. I accepted it. My family accepted it.

155
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:30,999
Now I have something else I want to share. My husband was already a non-Christian. We got married under the Special Marriage Act.

156
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:39,999
We studied together. We have known each other for 24 years. This year will be our 25th year together, and we’ve been married for 15 years.

157
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:45,999
As I mentioned earlier, I come from the Jacobite Syrian Christian Church. So my family didn’t accept this relationship in any way.

158
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:50,999
But I was adamant — maybe because of my age or the time in life — so they thought, “Let her do as she pleases,” and let it go.

159
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:56,999
But for me, having a church wedding was a dream. That dream didn’t come true back then.

160
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:03,999
During those days, when we were in love, I once asked him: “Will you become a Christian so we can get married in a church? That’s my wish.”

161
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:08,999
And he replied in a joking manner, “Now? Why suddenly?” But I took it very seriously.

162
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:13,999
For me, living a Christian life was very important. But maybe he hadn’t taken it that seriously.

163
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:23,999
Maybe at that age, he just thought: “If I say OK, she’ll move forward with this. Otherwise, she might leave me.”

164
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:36,999
So maybe he just said “OK” out of convenience back then. But that stuck in my heart, and that’s why I continued the relationship, introduced him to my family, and so on.

165
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:43,999
When it came time for marriage, he already had a daughter. And a church wedding or religious conversion would create complications for her.

166
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,999
Naturally, changing religion and getting married in a church would come with risks.

167
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:53,999
I understood that. I didn’t want to trouble him or his family. So I didn’t insist.

168
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,999
I said, “Okay, let’s just go ahead with the Special Marriage Act.” I didn’t push for a church wedding.

169
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:05,999
But still, deep inside, for many years, I’ve carried this dream in my heart — to have a church wedding. I’ve longed for it.

170
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:12,999
But I never told anyone. It’s been 15 years since we got married. And only after I made this covenant did things start to move.

171
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:22,999
After all these miracles took place, my husband came to faith. He himself said, “Let’s have our wedding in church.”

172
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:27,999
The same words he had jokingly said 24 years ago became real.

173
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:38,999
For the past 15 years, I’ve always gone to church alone. I used to think in my heart, “Lord, I’m not able to come with my family… not even with my children.”

174
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:44,999
But this month, I resigned from my job — because I got the visa. After returning, we had our church wedding.

175
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:49,999
Now, we are moving forward in Christian life as a family — my husband, my children, and I.

176
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:56,999
I can now go to church and receive the Holy Mass with my family. I’m filled with joy.

177
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:04,999
No matter how much I thank Mother Mary and Jesus, it will never be enough. I am so grateful for this chance.

178
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:10,999
During the time of war, I couldn’t leave the place. I had to stay back — but even that, I say, was part of Mother Mary’s miracle.

179
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:22,999
The patient I had been caring for... I was very attached to her. It’s now been 12 years that I’ve worked there.

180
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,999
And for 9.5 years, I’ve been looking after the same patient.

181
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:32,999
That elderly woman had deep love for me. She used to say, “Princey, if you go, I’ll die.”

182
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,999
She once had a heart attack. When I came home for a short visit, I was deeply disturbed —

183
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:42,999
thinking, “What if something happens to her while I move to another country?”

184
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,999
That’s one reason I kept postponing my plans to be with my family. She was 86 years old.

185
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:55,999
I kept delaying everything — because I felt I couldn’t bear the pain if she passed away after I left.

186
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:01,999
She cared for me like a mother. When I had a fever, instead of me helping her, she would make me black tea.

187
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:08,999
She was a Jewish lady with so much love.

188
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:15,999
When my second child was born and I went home to drop him off, that Jewish grandmother told me:

189
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:22,999
“Don’t travel alone. You can’t manage the baby alone on the flight. I’ll come with you.”

190
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:32,999
That woman, who hadn’t flown in 40 years, who walked only with a walker or cane inside the house,

191
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,999
who needed my help to even get around —

192
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:40,999
she got on the flight with me at the age of 86.

193
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:48,999
She stayed one week at my home. That’s how much love she had for me.

194
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:53,999
After staying a week, she left. And two months later, I followed — after settling my son.

195
00:19:54,000 --> 00:20:00,999
When I finally got my visa to New Zealand, I had to leave that beloved grandmother behind.

196
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:06,999
I was in deep heartbreak; even though I got the visa, I couldn’t feel happy because of the constant tension about whether they would pass away.

197
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:13,999
At that time, this grandmother told me it would be the last time she would see me.

198
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,999
She said, “Princey, I have no life left; I am finished.”

199
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:25,999
I talked to her children and doctors, and they said because I stayed so long, there was a very high chance something might happen to her.

200
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:31,999
They said there’s a 90% chance she might pass away since she depends on me so much.

201
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,999
I prayed to Mother Mary, “Mother, please perform a miracle.”

202
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:44,999
Jincy had given me a pinch of salt, so I put that salt in the water grandmother drinks, praying, “Mother, please give her courage and strength.”

203
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:58,999
Then grandmother should say, “You should go ahead and live with your family. It’s okay. I’m old now, I can adjust to living with someone else.”

204
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:05,999
I prayed, cried, and gave her the water to drink.

205
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,999
The next morning she got up and did her prayers as usual.

206
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:19,999
After that, I told her about my future plans and my wish to get married in the church when I return home.

207
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:33,999
She said, “Go ahead. I can adjust with someone else. Don’t be afraid. Be brave. No one will be like you to me, but you have a good life ahead.”

208
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:40,999
“I don’t want you to be selfish, so be brave and go. We will find someone else to care for me.”

209
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:50,999
By God’s grace, I prayed, “Mother, please find someone better than me to care for grandmother. Only then can I leave happily.”

210
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,999
I handed in my resignation letter.

211
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:05,999
On the fourth day, my family said, “There’s a staff member. Let’s interview her. If you like her, we can confirm.”

212
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,999
She came — someone almost like me.

213
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:13,999
Grandmother doesn’t like many people; she has very particular ways.

214
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:18,999
But after meeting this lady, grandmother liked her very much.

215
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:24,999
By God’s providence, I found an Indian nurse who was very kind.

216
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:29,999
I explained everything — how to care for grandmother, what to do.

217
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,999
I had already handed in my resignation letter, hopeful and expecting good things ahead.

218
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:37,999
She did everything perfectly. God gave me this person just when I needed her.

219
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:45,999
Because of the earlier date I gave, I was able to leave my job earlier than planned, so I could reach India on time.

220
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:51,999
I resigned early because I hadn’t found a replacement yet.

221
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:57,999
During the intense war with Iran, I got caught in the middle of the conflict.

222
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:03,999
I couldn’t travel to New Zealand because the airports there were all closed.

223
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:09,999
It was a very heavy attack; everyone must have seen it, even in New Zealand.

224
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:15,999
But God had a plan — a great plan for me and my family.

225
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:21,999
I cannot thank Him enough. Many things I longed for in my life —

226
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:29,999
my marriage that didn’t happen earlier, and the family life I lacked — He granted all of them to me.

227
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:35,999
I got the opportunity to study credit courses in New Zealand, and now I can bring my husband and children with me.

228
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,999
I thank God deeply.

229
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:47,999
Because of my evangelical work, I couldn’t go out much or do many things since I care for a single patient.

230
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:54,999
I had already given money to poor people who needed financial help, and I helped them.

231
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:02,999
My husband also cooks at an old age home back home and helps the poor.

232
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:08,999
After entering this faith through the covenant, we started distributing the Kreupasanam newsletter to everyone.

233
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:23,999
I also began sharing my father’s meditations and other things online as best as I could.

234
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:27,999
So my family is growing well in faith.

235
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:32,999
We are very happy and thankful to God for leading my family forward in Christian life.

236
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:40,999
We have Mass and worship; in every way, we are living as Christians now.

237
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:46,999
Psalm 84, verses 4 and 5 say, “Blessed are those who dwell in your house; they are ever praising you.”

238
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:49,999
“Blessed are those who find strength in you.”

239
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:56,999
“They have hearts set on pilgrimage to Zion, through the mediation of the Holy Mother.”

240
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:04,999
Princey and Jince have made a covenant with Jesus through the intercession of the Holy Mother, and today they shared their testimony of this revelation.

241
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:13,999
Through this testimony, we understand how the Holy Mother cared for Prince long ago.

242
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:22,999
She united them and blessed their marriage with great joy that none else can match.

243
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:32,999
Through this testimony, we see how she brought them together and how great their marriage is, beyond any comparison.

244
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:40,999
This testimony shows us that they were united and strengthened in a deep, unbreakable love of God that no one else could separate.

245
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:46,999
Many of us now understand from these recent testimonies what’s happening.

246
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:53,999
If 20 people have given testimonies, at least two of them will have faced trolls.

247
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:59,999
But those who know about trolls are the ones giving very powerful testimonies.

248
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,999
We realize that even those who mocked or left negative comments about the trolls

249
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:13,999
have become strong witnesses of faith themselves.

250
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:21,999
This holy Mother appearing at the altar gives such powerful testimonies.

251
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:27,999
Even the trolls are very positive toward Kreupasanam Mother because no one can defeat the Holy Mother.

252
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:34,999
This is God’s plan, and as Josephchan says, it’s not just empty prayers or talk — it is active work.

253
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:40,999
It is the work of the Holy Mother’s intercession, a way of life, a lifestyle.

254
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:48,999
This daughter who has lived continuously in Israel for 11 years came into Kreupasanam as a friend.

255
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:54,999
All of us have a friend or someone — maybe a Kreupasanam newsletter, some holy oil here —

256
00:26:55,000 --> 00:27:00,999
that has entered our lives through the Holy Mother’s intercession.

257
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:08,999
Thus this daughter grew to become a vessel of the great love of the Mother.

258
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:13,999
“Luther is a vessel of love” is a title related to the Holy Mother.

259
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:23,999
Just like the Holy Mother, we are given a great opportunity to stay connected to her through becoming members of Kreupasanam.

260
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:28,999
Let us thank Jesus and the Holy Mother. When we take the covenant,

261
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:34,999
all the small things and lost documents from years ago come back to us.

262
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:41,999
In 2008, this sister lost a bank transaction, but through the Holy Mother’s intercession,

263
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:50,999
it was resolved within 24 hours.

264
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:58,999
At the Cana wedding feast, there was only a single moment to make the wine —

265
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:05,999
let God’s name be glorified. As He said, the Holy Mother removed disgrace and shame from that wedding feast,

266
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:10,999
and she remains our greatest support.

267
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:18,999
Likewise, when we do acts of mercy, we should always reflect and ask,

268
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,999
“Are our merciful acts genuine?” We must not neglect our missionary work.

269
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:25,999
Am I giving Jesus to others? How much have I accepted Jesus? That much will be given to me.

270
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:32,999
We need to think and reflect on whether we are truly able to give to others what we have received.

271
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:40,999
This sister shared with us that while caring for an elderly lady at her workplace,

272
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:47,999
handing over the responsibility to someone else was a profound experience for her,

273
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,999
more than just a duty—it became an act of mercy and love.

274
00:28:55,000 --> 00:29:00,999
The love we receive through the Holy Mother is the answer to everything. Let us thank the Holy Mother and Jesus.

275
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:07,999
Let us place our lives in the hands of the Holy Mother. When we take the covenant,

276
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:13,999
the assurance we get from the Holy Mother is what Jesus gives us. Jesus always asks us to love the Holy Mother, His own mother.

277
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:19,999
At the foot of the cross, Jesus looked at Mary and John and said at the last moment,

278
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:25,999
“Woman, behold your son. Son, behold your mother.” Let us lovingly embrace the Mother given to us,

279
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:31,999
and stay united with Jesus. For the beautiful testimony of Princey and Jince

280
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:37,999
Jesus and the Holy Mother have given a warm applause. Let us offer our witness.

281
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:47,999
For more extraordinary spiritual experiences, if you haven’t subscribed to this YouTube channel yet, please do it now.

282
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:55,999
Share this video with your friends and become messengers of the Lord.

283
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
[Music]
